A banner above a procedure closed C-style: the comment runs on to the
first `;`, which ends the :PROCEDURE line, so the declaration is inside
the comment. comment_swallows_code (warning) names the swallowed
fragment; the orphaned :ENDPROC then surfaces as unmatched_block_end,
the puzzling symptom the catalog rationale describes
(diag.comment_swallows_code).
-- input.ssl --
/* Helper: trims and upper-cases a code
*/
:PROCEDURE CleanCode;
	:PARAMETERS sCode;
	:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sCode));
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/* Helper: trims and upper-cases a code
*/
:PROCEDURE CleanCode;
:PARAMETERS sCode;

:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sCode));
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-3:22 warning comment_swallows_code: This comment does not end at its '*/' - SSL comments end at ';', so it runs on and swallows ':PROCEDURE CleanCode'. That code never executes. End the comment with ';'
6:1-6:9 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDPROC' without matching block start
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-3:22 warning comment_swallows_code: This comment does not end at its '*/' - SSL comments end at ';', so it runs on and swallows ':PROCEDURE CleanCode'. That code never executes. End the comment with ';'
6:1-6:9 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDPROC' without matching block start
